      "side": 1,
      "message": "I interpreted the existing `context.okay` approach has being a kind of \"--keep-going\", to collect several errors before failing. If we\u0027re going to fail fast, why not just do away with `context.okay` and use `panic` ?",
      "revId": "4b37af5faca1c818cebff3e5e89c970766c6acc1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
