        "id": 1903985
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T16:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Graceful in a few ways:\n1. There won\u0027t multiple stack traces in the event of an error\n2. Instead of a worker go-routine panicking, it lets the parent context determine what it wants to do (e.g. any clean-up or logging for instance)\n3. Were one to add unit tests for this (as one should), not using panic would probably be more test-friendly.",
      "parentUuid": "ccbb6f8a_79c7e091",
